## Why This Is Asked

Explores a fresh angle on concurrency: multi-tenant in-order processing with a degradation path that preserves correctness while boosting throughput under pressure.

## Key Concepts

- Per-client FIFO buffers
- Global bounded queue and backpressure
- Degradation path that preserves per-client order
- Graceful shutdown and observability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code sketch for routing with per-client ordering
class Router {
  constructor() {
    this.clients = new Map();
    this.global = new BoundedQueue(100);
    this.workers = new WorkerPool(4);
  }

  enqueue(clientId, item) {
    let q = this.clients.get(clientId) ?? new Queue();
    q.enqueue(item);
    this.clients.set(clientId, q);
    if (!this.global.isFull()) {
      this.global.enqueue({ clientId, item: q.peek() });
    }
  }

  dequeueForWorker() {
    // pick from current head of a client, then next in round-robin
  }
}
```

